<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Net Irish forex intervention close to zero in 1996.</title>
<headline>Net Irish forex intervention close to zero in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net interventions on the foreign exchange market were close to zero in 1996 although Ireland's Central Bank said it intervened in both directions in occasionally volatile market conditions to smooth the movements of the Irish pound.</p>
<p>In its quarterly bulletin published on Thursday, the bank said the official external reserves fell by around 500 million Irish pounds to just under five billion, largely as a result of valuation changes.  </p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
